---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What is a Content Creator Rate Calculator and how does it work?",
    answer: "A Content Creator Rate Calculator is a professional financial estimating tool designed for freelance creators, videographers, photographers, copywriters, and UGC specialists. It calculates project quotes using two industry-standard methodologies: an Hourly/Project Labor model (accounting for pre-production, shooting, editing, expenses, and revisions) and a Deliverables Package model (accounting for asset volume discounts and commercial paid usage licensing)."
  },
  {
    question: "How do I calculate my freelance content creator hourly rate?",
    answer: "To calculate your hourly rate, determine your desired annual personal take-home income, add annual business overhead expenses (software, camera gear, insurance, accounting) and a 25% to 30% self-employment tax buffer. Then divide that total by your realistic annual billable hours (typically 1,000 to 1,200 billable hours per year, as roughly 40% of your time is spent on non-billable administration and marketing)."
  },
  {
    question: "What is the standard price for User-Generated Content (UGC) videos?",
    answer: "Standard baseline rates for a single 30-to-60-second UGC video range between $150 and $350 for beginner to intermediate creators with organic usage. For experienced creators delivering concept ideation, professional lighting, hooks, and 90-day paid ad whitelisting rights, UGC rates typically range from $400 to $1,000+ per video."
  },
  {
    question: "Why should creators charge extra for commercial paid ad usage rights?",
    answer: "Organic posting fees cover content shared to an existing audience or organic brand feed. When a brand runs your content as a paid targeted advertisement (Meta Ads, TikTok Spark Ads), they generate direct revenue and scale impressions from your likeness and creative work. Charging an additional 20% to 75%+ usage licensing fee compensates you for the commercial value generated."
  },
  {
    question: "How should creators handle project revisions and scope creep?",
    answer: "Standard creator agreements should include one round of minor revisions (e.g., minor audio tweaks or caption adjustments). Extra revision rounds or major script changes requested after filming should carry a dedicated revision surcharge (standardly $50 to $150 per round or your standard hourly rate) to protect your schedule."
  },
  {
    question: "What is the difference between hourly pricing and package-based pricing?",
    answer: "Hourly pricing charges clients for the exact time spent scripting, shooting, and editing, making it ideal for consulting or complex post-production. Package-based pricing charges a fixed fee per asset bundle (e.g., 3 short-form videos and 5 photos), providing clients with predictable costs and allowing creators to earn higher effective hourly rates through efficient workflows."
  },
  {
    question: "How much of a deposit should creators require before starting work?",
    answer: "Professional creators should always require a 50% non-refundable upfront deposit upon contract signing before beginning pre-production, with the remaining 50% balance due upon delivery of the watermarked final draft prior to releasing raw unwatermarked assets."
  },
  {
    question: "How can creators transition from one-off projects to monthly retainers?",
    answer: "Creators can propose recurring monthly packages (e.g., 4 dedicated short-form videos and 8 photos per month for a 3-to-6-month commitment) at a 10% to 15% bundle discount compared to one-off pricing. This gives the brand consistent content velocity while providing the creator with predictable monthly recurring revenue."
  }
];
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Content Creator Rate Calculator - Freelance Pricing & Quote Estimator"
  description="Calculate your freelance content creator rates, UGC pricing, and project quotes. Free online calculator for hourly labor pricing or deliverables package quotes."
  toolName="Content Creator Rate Calculator"
  toolDescription="Generate custom content creator pricing. Toggle between Hourly/Project labor calculations or Deliverables Package structures to build professional quotes."
  category="Calculators"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <div slot="calculator" class="calc-card glass">
    <!-- Calculator Mode selector tabs -->
    <div class="calculator-mode-selector" role="tablist" aria-label="Pricing Model">
      <button type="button" class="mode-tab active" data-mode="hourly" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="calc-form-container">
        <span>Hourly / Project Rate</span>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="mode-tab" data-mode="package" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="calc-form-container">
        <span>Deliverables Package</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="calc-grid" id="calc-form-container">
      <!-- Input fields -->
      <form class="calc-form" id="creator-rate-form" onsubmit="return false;">
        <input type="hidden" id="active-mode" value="hourly" />

        <!-- Hourly Mode Inputs -->
        <div id="inputs-hourly-box" class="inputs-group">
          <div class="form-row-2">
            <div class="form-group">
              <div class="label-header">
                <label for="hourly-rate" class="icon-label">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="field-icon">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 6v6h4.5m4.5 0a9 9 0 1 1-18 0 9 9 0 0 1 18 0Z" />
                  </svg>
                  Target Hourly Rate ($)
                </label>
              </div>
              <input type="number" id="hourly-rate" class="form-input" placeholder="e.g., 50" min="10" step="1" required />
            </div>

            <div class="form-group">
              <div class="label-header">
                <label for="hours-pre" class="icon-label">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="field-icon">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M16.862 4.487 1.687-1.688a1.875 1.875 0 1 1 2.652 2.652L10.582 16.07a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-1.897 1.13L6 18l.8-2.685a4.5 4.5 0 0 1 1.13-1.897l8.932-8.931Zm0 0L19.5 7.125M18 14v4.75A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 15.75 21H5.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 3 18.75V8.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 5.25 6H10" />
                  </svg>
                  Pre-Prod Hours (Scripting, Prep)
                </label>
              </div>
              <input type="number" id="hours-pre" class="form-input" placeholder="e.g., 2" min="0" step="0.5" value="1" />
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="form-row-2">
            <div class="form-group">
              <div class="label-header">
                <label for="hours-production" class="icon-label">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="field-icon">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6.827 6.175A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 5.186 7.23c-.38.054-.757.112-1.134.175C2.999 7.58 2.25 8.507 2.25 9.574V18a2.25 2.25 0 0 0 2.25 2.25h15A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 21.75 18V9.574c0-1.067-.75-1.994-1.802-2.169a47.865 47.865 0 0 0-1.134-.175 2.31 2.31 0 0 1-1.64-1.055l-.822-1.316A2.192 2.192 0 0 0 14.53 4H9.47c-.527 0-1.026.262-1.332.712l-.822 1.316Z" /><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 16.5a3.75 3.75 0 1 0 0-7.5 3.75 3.75 0 0 0 0 7.5Z" />
                  </svg>
                  Production Hours (Filming, Shooting)
                </label>
              </div>
              <input type="number" id="hours-production" class="form-input" placeholder="e.g., 4" min="0" step="0.5" value="2" />
            </div>

            <div class="form-group">
              <div class="label-header">
                <label for="hours-post" class="icon-label">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="field-icon">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10.5 6a7.5 7.5 0 1 0 7.5 7.5h-7.5V6Z" /><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 10.5H21A7.5 7.5 0 0 0 13.5 3v7.5Z" />
                  </svg>
                  Post-Prod Hours (Editing, Audio)
                </label>
              </div>
              <input type="number" id="hours-post" class="form-input" placeholder="e.g., 3" min="0" step="0.5" value="2" />
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="form-row-2">
            <div class="form-group">
              <div class="label-header">
                <label for="project-expenses" class="icon-label">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="field-icon">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.25 18.75a60.07 60.07 0 0 1 15.797 2.101c.727.198 1.453-.342 1.453-1.096V18.75M3.75 4.5h16.5M4.5 19.5h15M12 6.75v10.5m-3.75-3h7.5" />
                  </svg>
                  Direct Expenses ($) (Props, Travel)
                </label>
              </div>
              <input type="number" id="project-expenses" class="form-input" placeholder="e.g., 50" min="0" step="1" value="0" />
            </div>

            <div class="form-group">
              <div class="label-header">
                <label for="revision-rounds" class="icon-label">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="field-icon">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M16.023 9.348h4.992v-.001M2.985 19.644v-4.992m0 0h4.992m-4.993 0 3.181 3.183a8.25 8.25 0 0 0 13.803-3.7M4.031 9.865a8.25 8.25 0 0 1 13.803-3.7l3.181 3.182m0-4.991v4.99" />
                  </svg>
                  Total Revisions (First 1 Free)
                </label>
              </div>
              <input type="number" id="revision-rounds" class="form-input" placeholder="e.g., 2" min="1" step="1" value="1" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Deliverables Package Mode Inputs (Hidden by default) -->
        <div id="inputs-package-box" class="inputs-group hidden">
          <div class="form-row-2">
            <div class="form-group">
              <div class="label-header">
                <label for="package-videos" class="icon-label">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="field-icon">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m15.75 10.5 4.72-4.72a.75.75 0 0 1 1.28.53v11.38a.75.75 0 0 1-1.28.53l-4.72-4.72M4.5 18.75h9a2.25 2.25 0 0 0 2.25-2.25v-9a2.25 2.25 0 0 0-2.25-2.25h-9A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 2.25 7.5v9a2.25 2.25 0 0 0 2.25 2.25Z" />
                  </svg>
                  Number of Videos
                </label>
              </div>
              <input type="number" id="package-videos" class="form-input" placeholder="e.g., 2" min="0" step="1" value="0" />
            </div>

            <div class="form-group">
              <div class="label-header">
                <label for="package-photos" class="icon-label">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="field-icon">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6.827 6.175A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 5.186 7.23c-.38.054-.757.112-1.134.175C2.999 7.58 2.25 8.507 2.25 9.574V18a2.25 2.25 0 0 0 2.25 2.25h15A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 21.75 18V9.574c0-1.067-.75-1.994-1.802-2.169a47.865 47.865 0 0 0-1.134-.175 2.31 2.31 0 0 1-1.64-1.055l-.822-1.316A2.192 2.192 0 0 0 14.53 4H9.47c-.527 0-1.026.262-1.332.712l-.822 1.316Z" /><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 16.5a3.75 3.75 0 1 0 0-7.5 3.75 3.75 0 0 0 0 7.5Z" />
                  </svg>
                  Number of Photos
                </label>
              </div>
              <input type="number" id="package-photos" class="form-input" placeholder="e.g., 5" min="0" step="1" value="0" />
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="form-row-2">
            <div class="form-group">
              <div class="label-header">
                <label for="package-copy" class="icon-label">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="field-icon">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 14.25v-2.625a3.375 3.375 0 0 0-3.375-3.375h-1.5A1.125 1.125 0 0 1 13.5 7.125v-1.5a3.375 3.375 0 0 0-3.375-3.375H8.25m0 12.75h7.5m-7.5 3H12M10.5 2.25H5.625c-.621 0-1.125.504-1.125 1.125v17.25c0 .621.504 1.125 1.125 1.125h12.75c.621 0 1.125-.504 1.125-1.125V11.25a9 9 0 0 0-9-9Z" />
                  </svg>
                  Number of Articles/Copy
                </label>
              </div>
              <input type="number" id="package-copy" class="form-input" placeholder="e.g., 1" min="0" step="1" value="0" />
            </div>

            <div class="form-group">
              <div class="label-header">
                <label for="package-usage" class="icon-label">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="field-icon">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75 11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12c0 1.268-.63 2.39-1.593 3.068a3.745 3.745 0 0 1-1.043 3.296 3.745 3.745 0 0 1-3.296 1.043A3.745 3.745 0 0 1 12 21c-1.268 0-2.39-.63-3.068-1.593a3.746 3.746 0 0 1-3.296-1.043 3.745 3.745 0 0 1-1.043-3.296A3.745 3.745 0 0 1 3 12c0-1.268.63-2.39 1.593-3.068a3.745 3.745 0 0 1 1.043-3.296 3.746 3.746 0 0 1 3.296-1.043A3.746 3.746 0 0 1 12 3c1.268 0 2.39.63 3.068 1.593a3.746 3.746 0 0 1 3.296 1.043 3.746 3.746 0 0 1 1.043 3.296A3.745 3.745 0 0 1 21 12Z" />
                  </svg>
                  Usage Rights Licensing
                </label>
              </div>
              <select id="package-usage" class="form-input">
                <option value="none" selected>Organic Usage Only (Free)</option>
                <option value="ad_30">30-Day Paid Ad Rights (+20%)</option>
                <option value="ad_90">90-Day Paid Ad Rights (+40%)</option>
                <option value="ad_365">365-Day Paid Ad Rights (+75%)</option>
                <option value="ad_perpetual">Perpetual Ad Rights (+150%)</option>
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Base Rate configuration overrides -->
          <div class="toggle-group" style="margin-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px dashed var(--color-border); padding-top: 1rem;">
            <label class="checkbox-container">
              <input type="checkbox" id="toggle-custom-rates" />
              <span class="checkbox-label">Override Default Asset Rates</span>
            </label>
          </div>

          <div id="custom-rates-box" class="form-row-2 hidden" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
            <div class="form-group">
              <label for="custom-video-rate" class="checkbox-label">Video Base ($)</label>
              <input type="number" id="custom-video-rate" class="form-input" placeholder="Default 150" min="10" />
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
              <label for="custom-photo-rate" class="checkbox-label">Photo Base ($)</label>
              <input type="number" id="custom-photo-rate" class="form-input" placeholder="Default 75" min="10" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="form-actions">
          <button type="button" id="calc-submit-btn" class="calc-btn" style="width: 100%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.5rem;">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" style="width: 18px; height: 18px;">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 6v12m-3-2.818.879.659c1.171.879 3.07.879 4.242 0 1.172-.879 1.172-2.303 0-3.182C13.536 12.219 12.768 12 12 12c-.725 0-1.45-.22-2.003-.659-1.106-.879-1.106-2.303 0-3.182s2.9-.879 4.006 0l.415.33M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-18 0 9 9 0 0 1 18 0Z" />
            </svg>
            Calculate Creator Rate
          </button>
          <button type="button" id="calc-reset-btn" class="calc-btn-secondary" style="width: 100%;">Reset Form</button>
        </div>
      </form>

      <!-- Outputs Display -->
      <div class="calc-results" id="results-wrapper">
        <div class="empty-state text-center" id="res-empty-box">
          <svg class="empty-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11.25 11.25l.041-.02a.75.75 0 11.708 1.32l-.042.02a.75.75 0 01-.707-1.32zm0-4.5l.041-.02a.75.75 0 11.708 1.32l-.042.02a.75.75 0 01-.707-1.32zM12 6.75v10.5M8.25 18.75h7.5" />
          </svg>
          <h3>Awaiting Price Parameters</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">Select your calculation model, input hours or deliverables, then click Calculate to review quotes.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="results-active hidden" id="res-active-box">
          <div class="rate-range-box">
            <h4 class="rate-label">Estimated Rate Quote</h4>
            <div class="rate-range" id="res-total-val">$0.00</div>
            <div class="grade-badge grade-low" id="res-range-val">$0 - $0 range</div>
          </div>

          <div class="breakdown-box">
            <h4 class="breakdown-title">Itemized Price Breakdown</h4>
            <div class="breakdown-list" id="res-breakdown-container">
              <!-- Rendered dynamically via JavaScript -->
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div slot="about" class="editorial-content">
    <h2>The Complete Guide to Content Creator Rates & Freelance Pricing</h2>
    <p>
      In the modern digital economy, content creation has evolved from an informal side-hustle into a high-demand professional service. From User-Generated Content (UGC) specialists and freelance video editors to brand photographers, graphic designers, and social media strategists, businesses increasingly rely on external creators to fuel their marketing funnels.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, one of the greatest obstacles freelance creators encounter is knowing <strong>how to calculate their creator rates</strong>. Underpricing leads to exhaustion, unpaid administrative hours, and financial instability. Conversely, quoting arbitrary numbers without a clear line-item rationale can cause prospective clients to hesitate or walk away.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our <strong>Content Creator Rate Calculator</strong> provides an objective, mathematical pricing framework. Whether you bill by the hour for custom production and editing or quote flat-rate deliverable packages with built-in volume discounts and paid ad licensing, this tool helps you establish profitable rates and quote clients with confidence.
    </p>

    <div class="callout-box">
      <div class="callout-title">
        <span>💡</span> Campaign Strategy & Rate Pitching
      </div>
      <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;">
        Looking to pitch high-ticket retainers and build irresistible media kits? Explore our companion strategic guide: <a href="/blog/content-creator-rate-calculator-guide">Content Creator Pricing Guides & Campaign Negotiation Strategies</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Different Pricing Models Used by Content Creators</h2>
    <p>
      Professional creators use various commercial pricing models depending on project complexity, asset type, and client relationship:
    </p>

    <div class="step-guide">
      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>1. Hourly Labor Pricing</h3>
        <p>
          You charge a fixed rate for each hour dedicated to the project. This model is best for open-ended creative tasks where the exact scope is unpredictable—such as long-form video editing, copywriting, channel consulting, and ongoing technical production.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>2. Per-Deliverable / Flat-Fee Asset Pricing</h3>
        <p>
          You charge a flat price per completed asset (e.g., $150 per short-form vertical video or $75 per edited product photo). Brands often prefer this model because it provides fixed budgetary certainty regardless of how long production takes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>3. Deliverables Package Bundling</h3>
        <p>
          Combining multiple assets into structured bundles (e.g., 3 TikTok videos + 10 product photos). Bundling incentivizes clients to commit to larger production orders while allowing creators to offer volume discounts (10% to 20%) that reward batch shooting efficiency.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>4. Monthly Retainer Agreements</h3>
        <p>
          A long-term contract where the client pays a fixed monthly fee in exchange for a guaranteed volume of deliverables (e.g., 4 videos and 8 photos per month on a 3-to-6-month agreement). Retainers provide creators with stable recurring revenue while saving brands the friction of ongoing creator sourcing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>5. User-Generated Content (UGC) vs Influencer Posting</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>UGC Creation:</strong> You produce high-converting assets exclusively for the brand to use on their official channels or paid ad campaigns (no requirement to post to your personal social channels).<br />
          <strong>Influencer Sponsorship:</strong> You charge for both the content creation AND distribution access to your established personal audience.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>6. Performance-Based & Hybrid Retainers</h3>
        <p>
          A hybrid compensation structure that pairs a baseline production fee with milestone performance bonuses (e.g., $1,000 base + $250 bonus if a video exceeds 50,000 views or a 10% affiliate commission on tracked sales).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Key Factors That Influence Content Creator Rates</h2>
    <p>
      Your market rate is determined by several core variables:
    </p>

    <div class="table-responsive-wrapper">
      <table class="content-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Influencing Factor</th>
            <th>Pricing Impact</th>
            <th>Industry Benchmark / Best Practice</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Production Quality & Gear</strong></td>
            <td>Higher Baseline Rates</td>
            <td>4K cinema/mirrorless cameras, professional lighting rigs, and studio audio justify 1.5x to 2x higher rates than basic smartphone recording.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Creator Experience & Portfolio</strong></td>
            <td>Premium Authority Multiplier</td>
            <td>Proven track records with high-converting hooks and established case studies allow creators to charge premium rates ($500+ per video).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Content Niche & Buyer Intent</strong></td>
            <td>High-LTV Multipliers</td>
            <td>Specialized niches (B2B SaaS, Finance, Tech, Medical Skincare) pay higher rates due to large customer lifetime values compared to general entertainment.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Commercial Paid Ad Usage Rights</strong></td>
            <td><strong>+20% to +150% Surcharge</strong></td>
            <td>Licensing content for paid social advertising (Meta Ads / TikTok Spark Ads) must be billed as an extra line item based on duration (30/90/365 days).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Expedited Turnaround (Rush Fees)</strong></td>
            <td><strong>+25% to +50% Surcharge</strong></td>
            <td>Projects requiring delivery in under 48 to 72 hours should carry a rush fee to compensate for disrupted production schedules.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Project Revisions</strong></td>
            <td>Fixed Surcharge Beyond Free Round</td>
            <td>One round of minor edits should be included; additional rounds or major script pivots must be billed at $50 to $100+ per round.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>How This Content Creator Rate Calculator Works</h2>
    <p>
      Our calculator features two distinct calculation engines built around standard freelance accounting frameworks:
    </p>

    <h3>Mode 1: Hourly / Project Labor Model</h3>
    <p>
      This model breaks down your production labor across the three essential phases of content creation:
    </p>
    <div class="formula-box">
      Labor Subtotal = (Pre-Production Hours + Production Hours + Post-Production Hours) × Target Hourly Rate
      <br />
      Revision Surcharge = Max(0, Total Revisions - 1) × $50.00
      <br />
      Total Project Quote = Labor Subtotal + Direct Expenses + Revision Surcharge
    </div>

    <h3>Mode 2: Deliverables Package Model</h3>
    <p>
      This model calculates asset bundling with automatic volume discounts and commercial usage licensing:
    </p>
    <div class="formula-box">
      Gross Asset Total = (Videos × Video Rate) + (Photos × Photo Rate) + (Articles × Article Rate)
      <br />
      Volume Discount = 10% (2–3 items) | 15% (4–5 items) | 20% (6+ items)
      <br />
      Discounted Subtotal = Gross Asset Total × (1 - Volume Discount)
      <br />
      Paid Ad Usage Premium = Discounted Subtotal × Usage Rate (30-day: +20%, 90-day: +40%, 365-day: +75%, Perpetual: +150%)
      <br />
      Total Package Quote = Discounted Subtotal + Paid Ad Usage Premium
    </div>

    <h2>Step-by-Step Guide: How to Use the Calculator Effectively</h2>
    <p>
      Follow this simple step-by-step workflow to generate an accurate price quote:
    </p>

    <div class="step-guide">
      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 1: Choose Your Calculation Mode</h3>
        <p>
          Click the tab at the top for <strong>Hourly / Project Rate</strong> (best for consulting, editing, and custom labor) or <strong>Deliverables Package</strong> (best for quoting specific quantities of videos, photos, and copy).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 2: Enter Labor Hours or Deliverable Quantities</h3>
        <p>
          <em>In Hourly Mode:</em> Input your target hourly rate, estimated pre-production hours (concepting/scripting), filming hours, and editing hours.<br />
          <em>In Package Mode:</em> Enter the exact quantity of videos, photos, or written articles requested by the brand.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 3: Factor in Expenses & Revisions</h3>
        <p>
          <em>In Hourly Mode:</em> Input direct out-of-pocket expenses (props, travel, studio rentals) and the total number of revision rounds requested.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 4: Configure Commercial Usage Licensing</h3>
        <p>
          <em>In Package Mode:</em> Select the usage rights duration from the dropdown menu (Organic Only, 30-Day, 90-Day, 365-Day, or Perpetual Paid Ad Rights).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 5: Optional - Custom Asset Rate Overrides</h3>
        <p>
          Check the <strong>Override Default Asset Rates</strong> box if you wish to adjust baseline asset rates ($150 for video, $75 for photos) to match your custom rate sheet.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 6: Review the Itemized Breakdown</h3>
        <p>
          Click <strong>Calculate Creator Rate</strong> to generate a complete itemized quote and review your suggested pricing range ($\pm15\%$ variance) to present to the client.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Realistic Rate Calculation Scenarios</h2>
    <p>
      To understand how these formulas apply in practice, review these four real-world creator pricing scenarios:
    </p>

    <div class="step-guide">
      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Scenario A: Beginner UGC Creator (3 Short-Form TikTok/Reels with 90-Day Ad Rights)</h3>
        <p><strong>Deliverables:</strong> 3 Vertical Video Ads | <strong>Usage:</strong> 90-Day Paid Ad Whitelisting</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Gross Asset Value:</strong> 3 Videos × $150.00 = $450.00</li>
          <li><strong>Volume Discount:</strong> 10% Batch Discount on 3 items = -$45.00</li>
          <li><strong>Discounted Subtotal:</strong> $405.00</li>
          <li><strong>Paid Ad Licensing:</strong> +40% for 90-day ad usage = +$162.00</li>
          <li><strong>Total Quote:</strong> <strong>$567.00</strong> (Suggested Range: <strong>$480 – $650</strong>)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Scenario B: Freelance Video Editor (Dedicated Long-Form YouTube Edit)</h3>
        <p><strong>Labor:</strong> 2 hrs Prep/Review + 6 hrs Video Editing/Color + 2 Revision Rounds @ $60.00/hr</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Labor Cost:</strong> 8 Total Hours × $60.00/hr = $480.00</li>
          <li><strong>Revision Surcharge:</strong> (2 rounds - 1 free) × $50.00 = +$50.00</li>
          <li><strong>Plugin & Asset Expenses:</strong> $50.00</li>
          <li><strong>Total Project Quote:</strong> <strong>$580.00</strong> (Suggested Range: <strong>$495 – $665</strong>)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Scenario C: Commercial Photographer (Product Photoshoot Bundle with Annual Ad Rights)</h3>
        <p><strong>Deliverables:</strong> 10 Edited High-Res Product Photos + 2 Short-Form Videos | <strong>Usage:</strong> 365-Day Paid Ad Rights</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Gross Asset Value:</strong> (10 Photos × $75) + (2 Videos × $150) = $1,050.00</li>
          <li><strong>Volume Discount:</strong> 20% Discount for 12 total items = -$210.00</li>
          <li><strong>Discounted Subtotal:</strong> $840.00</li>
          <li><strong>Paid Ad Licensing:</strong> +75% for 365-day commercial ad rights = +$630.00</li>
          <li><strong>Total Quote:</strong> <strong>$1,470.00</strong> (Suggested Range: <strong>$1,250 – $1,690</strong>)</li>
